From a7cc62c2e29629f8956758468dcf4996aa753710 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexey Lapin <a.lapin03@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:58:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] feat: add a guide mode for the Hone booth demo

A visitor at the booth can walk through the offer letter scenario alone.
A card names each step, outlines the control to use and moves on when the
real event happens, from opening a prepared chat to the new AGENTS.md
version. The guide writes the request and the feedback word for word as
the recorded visit had them.

The Hone dashboard in the Hone page's frame posts its route, Start
optimization and the start and end of a run to t3code, and t3code asks it
to outline the next control. Both sides check the other's origin.

After a short idle the booth video plays. After a long idle the guide
resets the demo. The Guide button in the sidebar turns guide mode on, and
leaving it takes a two second hold and the PIN when HONE_GUIDE_PIN is set.
hone.status carries the guide settings, and hone.guideUnlock checks the PIN.
